  "ResearchDossier": {
    "topic": "Cyber Monday was invented by a press release",
    "summary": "The term Cyber Monday was coined by Ellen Davis of the National Retail Federation's Shop.org in a press release on November 28, 2005, based on 2004 research that the Monday after Thanksgiving was one of the biggest online shopping days, as people returned to fast internet connections at work. Historically it had been about the 12th-biggest day. By 2020 it was the biggest online shopping day in US history, with $10.7 billion in online spending.",
    "angle": "A marketing name that made itself true.",
